{"text": "August 3, 1984\n\nTO: EB. R. Hardman\n\nRE: DORAL ACTION STANDARDS/PRODUCT TESTING\n\nThis confirms yesterday's conversation regarding\nDORAL product testing:\n\nChange in Action Standard. Given our discussions\nwith R&D and Brand's subsequent discussion with\nJ. T. Winebrenner, DORAL action standards will\nbe changed from superiority performance to parity\nperformance. All other elements of the action\nstandard will remain constant per our previous\nconversation. For further clarification, incor-\nporating this revision into the Filter 85's\naction standard, the new statement will read as\nfollows:\n\nAchieve parity versus Liggett Generics,\nwith cork tipping and 12-15 mg tar, among\nnon-menthol 85mm smokers of brands with\n11-17 mg tar who are 18 years of age or\nolder who have ever tried Generics.\n\nCompetitive product pickup. Brand requests, to the\nSstent possible, cometitive product carrying the\nsame \"brand name\" be utilized for product testing\nacross the four DORAL brand styles. However, this\nis not a hard and fast rule. As such, in keeping\nwith the action standards, all competitive generic\nproduct must be cork tipped in compliance with\nDORAL cork tipping. Therefore, if you must go out-\nside the \"brand name\" family to get cork tipping\non one or more competitive styles, Brand agrees to\ndo so.\n\nEd, I hope this clarifies Brand's direction on\nproduct testing. Please let me know your requested\nproduct testing dates as soon as they are formalized.\nBrand appreciates your diligence and patience in the\nnumerous discussions recently held surrounding prod-\nuct testing issues.\n\nMany thanks.\n\nJIG/adh\ncc: J. T. Winebrenner\nD. W. Shouse\nG. C. Eskridge\nL. 3. Inman\n\n\u201cA\n\n1649 SOEOS", "words": [{"text": "August", "x0": 431, "y0": 100, "x1": 487, "y1": 121, "conf": 92.0}, {"text": "3,", "x0": 499, "y0": 108, "x1": 513, "y1": 121, "conf": 92.0}, {"text": "1984", "x0": 527, "y0": 108, "x1": 562, "y1": 119, "conf": 89.0}, {"text": "TO